<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rocroi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1643</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Rocroi · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rocroi was fought in 1643 in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War, where a French army under the Duke of Enghien defeated the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-flanders">Army of Flanders</a>. The Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tercio">tercios</a>, long considered the finest infantry in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, suffered heavy losses. The battle is widely seen as marking the end of the military dominance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rocroi.jpg" alt="Battle of Rocroi" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sauveur Lecomte · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Bataille_de_Rocroi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
